# CareerForge — Module-Wise Categorization

---

## Module 1: The Cognitive Screener (Resume Engine)

### Master Form (1)
| Form | Insert | Delete | Update | Search | Display |
|------|--------|--------|--------|--------|---------|
| Student Profile | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |

### Transaction Forms (3)
| Form | Insert | Delete | Update | Search | Display |
|------|--------|--------|--------|--------|---------|
| Resume Upload | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
| Resume Analysis | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
| Career Path Generation | ✅ | — | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |

### Master Tables (2)
| Table | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| Users | Stores user credentials and roles |
| Job_Descriptions | Market job roles and requirements |

### Transaction Tables (3)
| Table | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| Resumes | Stores resume file metadata |
| Resume_Parsed_Data | Extracted skills, education, experience |
| Resume_Scores | AI-generated resume and job-fit scores |

### Report
Resume Analysis Report — AI-generated quality score, ATS compatibility, extracted skills, and improvement suggestions

### Visualization
Resume Score Breakdown — Overall score progress bar + expandable category-wise score cards

### API
[resume.routes.ts](file:///c:/Users/naren/OneDrive/Desktop/SEM-6/FFS%27/CareerForge/backend/api-gateway/src/routes/resume.routes.ts) — POST `/upload`, GET `/`, GET [/:id](file:///c:/Users/naren/OneDrive/Desktop/SEM-6/FFS%27/CareerForge/backend/api-gateway/src/routes/job.routes.ts#9-21), POST `/:id/reanalyze`, DELETE [/:id](file:///c:/Users/naren/OneDrive/Desktop/SEM-6/FFS%27/CareerForge/backend/api-gateway/src/routes/job.routes.ts#9-21), POST `/:id/analyze`, GET `/:id/analysis`, GET `/:id/skill-gaps`, GET `/:id/job-matches`
[career.routes.ts](file:///c:/Users/naren/OneDrive/Desktop/SEM-6/FFS%27/CareerForge/backend/api-gateway/src/routes/career.routes.ts) — Career path and skill roadmap generation
[user.routes.ts](file:///c:/Users/naren/OneDrive/Desktop/SEM-6/FFS%27/CareerForge/backend/api-gateway/src/routes/user.routes.ts) — Profile GET/PUT

### Testing
Frontend: Jest + React Testing Library | Backend: pytest + pytest-asyncio (ai-brain microservice)

